cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Unwind or ReversiBench in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "Unwind: A Reversibility Layer for Agentic Tool Use"
abstract: >-
  Unwind is a transparent Model Context Protocol (MCP) proxy that infers which
  agent tool calls are reversible (an ordinal R0-R4 taxonomy, assigned relative
  to the environment), synthesises inverse operations, maintains a durable
  cross-server undo log, and interrupts the human only for genuinely
  irreversible actions. Reversibility inference is the missing primitive that
  makes human oversight of agents sustainable by turning undifferentiated
  approval prompts into a meaningful signal.
type: software
